-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,2) size 704x39
-                        text run at (2,2) width 704: "When the Whiten house burned down in Renfrew Ontario, the insurer denied liability, asserting that the Plaintiff"
-                        text run at (2,22) width 468: "Daphne Whiten was the cause of the fire herself and had committed arson."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (470,37) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,42) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,62) size 751x79
-                        text run at (2,62) width 751: "The insurance company had not only refused to pay, but had received opinions from its adjuster, its expert engineer and"
-                        text run at (2,82) width 690: "an investigative agency that the fire was accidental. Its own adjuster had recommended the claim be paid. The"
-                        text run at (2,102) width 722: "defendant's counsel, as the court found, had pressured experts to provide opinions supporting an arson defence and"
-                        text run at (2,122) width 723: "withheld relevant information from the experts and gave them misleading information to buttress the arson defence."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (725,137) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,142) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,162) size 631x19
-                        text run at (2,162) width 631: "After the fire the Plaintiff and her husband, Keith Whiten needed welfare assistance to support them."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (632,177) size 1x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,182) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,202) size 732x59
-                        text run at (2,202) width 721: "The jury, however, in a 4 week trial, disagreed with the position of the insurance company. It awarded not only the"
-                        text run at (2,222) width 732: "policy sum against the insurer, but also was sufficiently annoyed with the conduct of the company to award a further"
-                        text run at (2,242) width 236: "punitive damage award of $1 million."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (238,257) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,262) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,282) size 751x59
-                        text run at (2,282) width 751: "The company appealed. At the time of the appeal, the company acknowledged that the fire was accidental. The Ontario"
-                        text run at (2,302) width 703: "Court of Appeal reversed the jury award and in a 2-1 decision determined that there should be a cap on punitive"
-                        text run at (2,322) width 140: "damages of $100,000."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (142,337) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,342) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,362) size 752x99
-                        text run at (2,362) width 752: "Lawyers became hard pressed to reconcile this decision with a prior case, Hill vs. Church of Scientology. Hill, a Crown"
-                        text run at (2,382) width 670: "Attorney, had sued the Church for libel due to statements made accusing him of breaching a judge's order. "
-                        text run at (671,382) width 20: "He"
-                        text run at (2,402) width 715: "succeeded. The jury at trial, aside from awarding compensatory damages, also awarded a punitive damage sum of"
-                        text run at (2,422) width 743: "$800,000. The decision was appealed without success to the Ontario Court of Appeal and again to the Supreme Court"
-                        text run at (2,442) width 514: "of Canada. The award of punitive damages was sustained at both appellate levels."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (516,457) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,462) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,482) size 749x59
-                        text run at (2,482) width 727: "In the Whiten case, the insurance industry is mounting all its ammunition to maintain the notion of a cap on punitive"
-                        text run at (2,502) width 749: "damages. It is expected that the Court of Appeal decision will receive a rough ride in the Supreme Court, given the Hill"
-                        text run at (2,522) width 166: "decision a few years prior."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (167,537) size 1x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,542) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,562) size 753x59
-                        text run at (2,562) width 725: "The concept of punitive damages is designed to act as civil penalty imposed on a wrong doer, which has conducted"
-                        text run at (2,582) width 753: "itself in a vindictive manner, which offends one's sense of propriety - high handed shocking behaviour. Traditionally the"
-                        text run at (2,602) width 729: "financial abilities of the wrong doer are a factor - the deeper the pockets the more substantial the sum to be awarded."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (731,617) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,622) size 0x19
-                      LayoutText {#text} at (2,642) size 745x99
-                        text run at (2,642) width 742: "Canadian courts have been reluctant to embrace the concept - awards such as Hill are rare. It is worthy of note that the"
-                        text run at (2,662) width 696: "dissenting reasons of Justice Laskin in Whiten were much in favour of maintaining the trial award - a lucid and"
-                        text run at (2,682) width 741: "powerful dissent written by a much respected jurist. Much attention will be given to this decision. Oral argument is set"
-                        text run at (2,702) width 745: "for the week of December 11th. A decision will likely be forthcoming in March to June time period. This decision will"
-                        text run at (2,722) width 499: "be no doubt a much quoted decision for many years, regardless of the outcome."
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (501,737) size 0x0
-                      LayoutBR {BR} at (2,742) size 0x19
